# oh-my-zsh — real-world examples

## Homelab: install zsh + oh-my-zsh on Tumbleweed

```sh
sudo zypper install zsh git curl
sh -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh/master/tools/install.sh)"
chsh -s "$(which zsh)"
```

## take — mkdir and cd in one step

```sh
# take my-project replaces mkdir my-project && cd my-project
take my-project
```

## zsh_stats — your top 20 commands by usage

```sh
zsh_stats
#  1  216  13.4%  ll
#  2  177  11.0%  cd
#  3   89   5.5%  vim
#  4   81   5.0%  git
#  ...
```

## cd shortcuts

| Alias | Effect           |
| ----- | ---------------- |
| ..    | 1 directory up   |
| ...   | 2 directories up |
| ....  | 3 directories up |
| ..... | 4 directories up |
| d     | list recently used directories; `cd -n` jumps to number n |

## Other built-in aliases

```sh
rd    # rmdir
md    # mkdir -p
```

Type `ls -` then hit Tab to list all options with explanations (works for cap, rake, ssh, kill, ...).

## Enable plugins and update

```sh
# In ~/.zshrc
plugins=(git sudo systemd)

# Update oh-my-zsh itself
omz update
```
